{
  "pattern": "overlayStack",
  "doc": "The layers floating above a screen (tooltips, menus, popovers, dialogs and sheets), in the order they opened. Escape, a press outside and Tab are decided here, once, so no screen handles them by hand.",
  "params": {},
  "state": {
    "layers": "Layer[]: bottom first. Layer = {id: string, kind: tooltip | menu | popover | dialog | sheet, parent: string | null (the layer that owns it: it closes with that layer), opener: string | null (the element focus returns to), openerLayer: string | null (the layer the opener is in; null for the screen)}"
  },
  "events": {
    "open": {
      "layer": "Layer"
    },
    "closed": {
      "id": "string: the owner has closed the layer",
      "openerPresent": "bool: the layer's opener, as the stack holds it now, is still on the page",
      "focus": "inside | lost | outside: where focus is as the layer closes: inside it (or in a layer it owns), lost (on the page body, or removed with the layer), or outside it (the user moved it)"
    },
    "escape": {
      "composing": "bool: an input method is composing text",
      "focusOwnsEscape": "bool: the focused control uses Escape itself (an open mention list or autocomplete, a message in edit mode)"
    },
    "pressOutside": {
      "insideId": "string | null: the innermost layer the press landed in, or null for the screen. A press on a popover's anchor counts as inside the popover"
    },
    "tab": {}
  },
  "effects": {
    "requestClose": {
      "id": "string",
      "reason": "escape | pressOutside | scrim | tab | parentClosed (a command: the owner must close it)"
    },
    "restoreFocus": {
      "to": "string | null: an element or layer id; null is the screen's own focus target"
    },
    "passToScreen": {
      "key": "Escape"
    }
  },
  "rules": [
    "Layers stack in the order they open. A tooltip always sits on top: a layer that opens while a tooltip is showing goes just below the tooltips.",
    "Opening a layer whose id is already in the stack does nothing.",
    "Escape asks the topmost layer to close: requestClose(topmost, 'escape'). Only one layer is asked per Escape, so nested layers close innermost first.",
    "A tooltip takes the Escape: Escape with tooltips on top asks each of them to close, topmost first, and goes no further. No other layer is asked, and the screen does not get the key.",
    "Escape with nothing open is passed to the screen: passToScreen('Escape'). The screen runs its own chain (close the docked panel, then mark as read).",
    "A press counts as inside a layer when it lands in that layer or in any layer it owns, however deep.",
    "A press outside a popover asks it to close (reason 'pressOutside') and carries on to the layers below.",
    "A press outside a menu asks it to close (reason 'pressOutside') and goes no further: the menu's invisible layer swallows it.",
    "A press outside a dialog or a sheet is a press on its scrim: requestClose(layer, 'scrim'), and it goes no further.",
    "A press never closes a tooltip. A tooltip closes when the pointer or focus leaves its control, which its owner handles.",
    "Tab while the topmost layer under the tooltips is a menu asks the menu to close (reason 'tab'). Otherwise Tab does nothing here, and focus moves as usual.",
    "requestClose is only a request: the owner may refuse it (a form with unsaved changes). A layer leaves the stack only when its owner reports closed.",
    "When a layer closes while layers it owns are still open, each of them gets requestClose with reason 'parentClosed', innermost first, and they leave the stack with it. parentClosed is a command, not a request: the owner must close the layer and may not refuse, and a later closed for it does nothing.",
    "When a layer closes with focus inside it or lost, focus goes to its opener if the owner reports the opener still on the page; otherwise to the layer the opener was in, if that is still open; otherwise to the screen (restoreFocus to null). When focus is outside the layer, because the user moved it there, focus does not move.",
    "Closing a tooltip moves no focus. closed for an id that is not in the stack does nothing.",
    "Focus is never restored beneath an open dialog or sheet: when a layer closes below a dialog or sheet that is still open, no restoreFocus is emitted.",
    "When a layer closes, every layer whose opener was inside it takes over the closed layer's opener and openerLayer. So a dialog opened from a menu item returns focus to the button that opened the menu.",
    "Escape while an input method is composing text never reaches the stack: escape with composing does nothing. A focused control that uses Escape itself gets it first: escape with focusOwnsEscape does nothing here.",
    "A layer opened with a parent or an openerLayer that is not in the stack is kept with that field set to null."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "escape closes the innermost first",
      "covers": [
        3,
        12,
        14
      ],
      "events": [
        {
          "open": {
            "layer": {
              "id": "d",
              "kind": "dialog",
              "parent": null,
              "opener": "deleteButton",
              "openerLayer": null
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "open": {
            "layer": {
              "id": "m",
              "kind": "menu",
              "parent": "d",
              "opener": "moreButton",
              "openerLayer": "d"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "escape": {
            "composing": false,
            "focusOwnsEscape": false
          }
        },
        {
          "closed": {
            "id": "m",
            "openerPresent": true,
            "focus": "inside"
          }
        },
        {
          "escape": {
            "composing": false,
            "focusOwnsEscape": false
          }
        },
        {
          "closed": {
            "id": "d",
            "openerPresent": true,
            "focus": "inside"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
